@icon("blocks")
system: section {
  | The parts of the system this spec talks about, each named by the role it plays as seen from
  | outside: what it reads, what it answers and what it reports. A rule references the part
  | whose behaviour it states, its subject; a part is no architecture: how it's built is the implementation's
  | business, not the spec's.
  |
  | Every part but the editor extension ships in the one `heron` command, so a laptop, a CI job
  | and an agent run the same parts at the same version; the extension runs that command.

  command_line: part {{
    The `heron` command: it reads its arguments, finds the [entry point](#language.core_format.files.entry_point), runs the commands
    registered for it and exits with a status that tells a script what happened.
  }}

  parser: part {{
    Reads a file's text into a lossless syntax tree and reports syntax errors, recovering so the
    rest of the file still parses.
  }}

  checker: part {{
    Loads an [entry point](#language.core_format.files.entry_point) and its includes and imports into one node tree, then resolves names,
    kinds, types and references across it and reports what breaks them.
  }}

  formatter: part {{
    Rewrites a file in its one canonical layout without changing what it means.
  }}

  linter: part {{
    Runs the lint rules over a checked tree and reports findings, each with the fixes that
    resolve it.
  }}

  prose_linter: part {{
    Projects a tree's prose into the regions a text linter reads and reports prose findings at
    their place in the source.
  }}

  interpreter: part {{
    Evaluates funcs, macros and expressions over a checked tree and runs tasks in order of
    their dependencies, recording each run: the task runner.
  }}

  generator: part {{
    Writes the files the generation targets of a checked tree produce, and tells when a written
    file is stale.
  }}

  language_server: part {{
    Answers an editor over the Language Server Protocol from the checked tree: diagnostics,
    completion, hover, navigation, renames, formatting and fixes.
  }}

  editor_grammar: part {{
    The tree-sitter grammar editors load to colour, fold and select Heron without starting the
    `heron` command.
  }}

  docs_generator: part {{
    Renders a tree as a static documentation site: a page per node, the API reference, search
    and the interactive parts each page loads; and as the Markdown files agents read.
  }}

  server: part {{
    Serves a workspace over HTTP: the spec browser and the same tree as Markdown files for
    agents.
  }}

  @display("VS Code extension")
  editor_extension: part {{
    The extension for VS Code and the editors built on it: it starts `heron lsp` as its
    language client, colours Heron before the server answers, shows the live preview beside
    the code and runs the `heron` commands.
  }}
}
